            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question_id": "sq:randomization:baseline-imbalance",
          "answer": "no",
          "justification": "Baseline table shows 27 versus 24 participants and only two conventional statistically significant differences among numerous characteristics: CWS and Sheehan scores. The investigators adjusted these measures; the report describes the groups as well matched apart from those differences. This pattern is compatible with chance, not strong evidence of a randomization failure.",
